WEBVTT

00:26:54.236 --> 00:27:00.116
So I mean, what we have is a lot
of progress on climate and, of course,

00:27:00.156 --> 00:27:05.476
technology around renewable energies
and around electric batteries

00:27:05.476 --> 00:27:06.756
and supply chain

00:27:06.756 --> 00:27:08.476
continue to get cheaper and cheaper

00:27:08.516 --> 00:27:10.716
as more money is being invested in it.

00:27:10.716 --> 00:27:16.036
And that does make me long-term
more optimistic that by 2045,

00:27:16.076 --> 00:27:19.876
a majority of the world's energy
will probably be coming from renewables.

00:27:19.916 --> 00:27:22.076
And five years ago,
I wouldn't have said that.

00:27:22.116 --> 00:27:25.516
But still, I mean, when the news today

00:27:25.516 --> 00:27:30.676
is that the Americans are sending
a high-level delegation to Caracas